From 7264a8a110c478818cb10f649e7e470372a07be9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiale Yao <yaojiale02@163.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:15:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: validate free-block response length

The free-block query reads the first response byte without checking that
the firmware returned any payload. A zero-length response can therefore
cause an out-of-bounds read.

Require the block-count byte before accessing it.

Fixes: bbc1d4154ec1 ("mt76: mt7915: add default calibrated data support")
Signed-off-by: Jiale Yao <yaojiale02@163.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261019101506.1926943-7-yaojiale02@163.com
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index 50587aff..c48be6b4 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -3003,6 +3003,10 @@ int mt7915_mcu_get_eeprom_free_block(struct mt7915_dev *dev, u8 *block_num)
 					&req, sizeof(req), true, &skb);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+	if (skb->len < sizeof(*block_num)) {
+		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 
 	*block_num = *(u8 *)skb->data;
 	dev_kfree_skb(skb);
